      "documentation": "Java method: static crop",
      "javadoc_description": "Crop a region from a RandomAccessibleInterval using (x, y, z) pixel coordinates.\n\nFor RAIs without axis metadata, assumes ZYX dimension order. Returns a view (no data copy) with the specified bounds, clamped to image bounds.\n\nImportant: This method assumes ZYX dimension order (dim0=Z, dim1=Y, dim2=X), which is common for OME-ZARR and N5 datasets. For images with different axis orders, wrap as ImgPlus with proper axis metadata and use `crop(ImgPlus, long[], long[], boolean)`.",
      "category": "Static Methods",
      "deprecated": false,
      "since_version": null,
      "see_also": [],
      "examples": []
    },
